---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/astro/Container.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Summary"
  description="A concise closing summary of the spec-driven enterprise context engineering presentation."
>
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden border-b border-ink-100 bg-paper">
    <div class="summary-aurora pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="summary-grain pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <Container width="wide" class="relative py-4 md:py-6">
      <!-- Title — anchored to the top of the page -->
      <h1
        class="display-balance mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center font-serif text-display-sm font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink-900 md:text-display"
      >
        The story this project
        <span class="mt-1 block italic text-accent">is really telling.</span>
      </h1>

      <!-- Ornamental divider -->
      <div
        class="mx-auto mt-10 flex w-full max-w-md items-center gap-3 md:mt-14"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-ink-200 to-transparent"
        ></span>
        <span class="text-sm text-accent">◆</span>
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-l from-transparent via-ink-200 to-transparent"
        ></span>
      </div>

      <!-- The two theses -->
      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-5xl space-y-12 md:mt-14 md:space-y-16">
        <!-- Thesis I — warm / accent · anchored left -->
        <article
          class="grid gap-6 md:max-w-3xl md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] md:items-start md:gap-12"
        >
          <p
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="font-serif text-7xl font-semibold italic leading-none tracking-tight text-accent/90 md:text-[8rem]"
          >
            I
          </p>
          <div>
            <p class="thesis-prose thesis-prose--warm">
              Hand building enterprise-ready agentic infrastructure from scratch
              <em class="thesis-emphasis thesis-emphasis--warm">forces</em>
              stakeholders to confront the friction between LLM behavior and enterprise constraints.
            </p>
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="mt-6 block h-px w-16 bg-gradient-to-r from-accent/70 to-transparent"
            ></span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Thesis II — cool / spruce · anchored right -->
        <article
          class="ml-auto grid gap-6 md:max-w-3xl md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,5rem)] md:items-start md:gap-12"
        >
          <div class="md:order-1 md:text-right">
            <p class="thesis-prose thesis-prose--cool md:ml-auto">
              End-to-end spec-driven development
              <em class="thesis-emphasis thesis-emphasis--cool">forces</em>
              ALL stakeholders to confront the security, compliance, governance, and reliability
              demands of deploying AI inside a real business.
            </p>
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="mt-6 block h-px w-16 bg-gradient-to-l from-spruce-700/70 to-transparent md:ml-auto"
            ></span>
          </div>
          <p
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="font-serif text-7xl font-semibold italic leading-none tracking-tight text-spruce-700/85 md:order-2 md:text-[8rem]"
          >
            II
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <!-- Closing rule -->
      <div
        class="mx-auto mt-14 flex w-full max-w-md items-center gap-3 md:mt-20"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-ink-200 to-transparent"
        ></span>
        <span class="text-[0.7rem] text-accent">◆</span>
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-l from-transparent via-ink-200 to-transparent"
        ></span>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section-sm md:py-section">
    <Container width="wide">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.2fr)_minmax(18rem,0.8fr)]">
        <article class="panel p-7 md:p-9">
          <p class="eyebrow text-accent">My argument</p>
          <p class="mt-5 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink-900 md:text-3xl">
            A custom orchestration layer is not extra architecture for its own sake. It is how an
            enterprise makes its own security, reliability, and business constraints unavoidable
            parts of the AI system.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
            Without that layer, the organization inherits someone else&rsquo;s assumptions about
            what matters, which sources count, when uncertainty is acceptable, and when a human
            needs to step in. My approach treats those questions as the core product problem.
          </p>
        </article>

        <aside class="rounded-[1.25rem] border border-accent/20 bg-accent-soft/45 p-7 shadow-soft">
          <p class="eyebrow text-accent">What changed</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
            The project reframes enterprise AI from &ldquo;give an agent more context&rdquo; to
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink-900">
              govern what context it receives, why it receives it, and what it may do next</strong
            >.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="summary-card">
          <span class="summary-card__number">01</span>
          <h2>Research</h2>
          <p>
            The landscape showed why generic context engines, long-context prompts, and naive RAG
            are not enough by themselves. Enterprise data carries authority, permissions, freshness,
            and political ownership.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="summary-card">
          <span class="summary-card__number">02</span>
          <h2>Approach</h2>
          <p>
            The proposed answer was spec-driven enterprise context engineering: a document stack,
            hybrid source-aware retrieval, scoped context bundles, domain agents, and a
            deterministic supervisor.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="summary-card">
          <span class="summary-card__number">03</span>
          <h2>Demo</h2>
          <p>
            The replay made the architecture visible. Each step retrieved only what it needed,
            produced structured output, passed through a supervisor gate, and either continued or
            halted safely.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div
        class="mt-8 rounded-[1.5rem] border border-ink-100 bg-ink-900 p-7 text-paper shadow-soft md:p-9"
      >
        <p class="eyebrow text-paper/55">The core lesson</p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(16rem,0.6fr)]">
          <p class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug text-paper md:text-3xl">
            The system should not feel magical. It should feel accountable.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/70">
            A complete run is valuable because every determination is traceable. An escalation is
            valuable because ambiguity is preserved instead of hidden. The win is not just
            automation; it is a workflow that business, legal, security, procurement, and
            engineering can all inspect and trust.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-center">
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl leading-snug text-ink-900">
          In short: this project argues that enterprise AI becomes useful when context is not merely
          retrieved, but <strong class="font-semibold text-accent">governed</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ----- Hero ambiance ---------------------------------------------------- */

  .summary-aurora {
    background:
      radial-gradient(72% 60% at 82% -4%, rgba(157, 87, 40, 0.22), transparent 62%),
      radial-gradient(56% 48% at 0% 22%, rgba(157, 87, 40, 0.1), transparent 64%),
      radial-gradient(70% 60% at 100% 78%, rgba(33, 71, 60, 0.18), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(76% 60% at 14% 100%, rgba(33, 71, 60, 0.1), transparent 70%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(252, 250, 245, 0) 0%, rgba(252, 250, 245, 0.55) 100%);
  }

  .summary-grain {
    background-image: radial-gradient(rgba(24, 33, 38, 0.06) 0.6px, transparent 0.7px);
    background-size: 18px 18px;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, black 28%, transparent 78%);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, black 28%, transparent 78%);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* ----- Two-thesis prose ------------------------------------------------- */

  .thesis-prose {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    font-family: 'Iowan Old Style', 'Palatino Linotype', 'Book Antiqua', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2vw, 2.15rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: -0.014em;
    color: #182126;
    max-width: 38rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Translucent ambient glow behind each thesis paragraph */
  .thesis-prose::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: -1.75rem -2.25rem;
    z-index: -1;
    border-radius: 999px;
    filter: blur(40px);
    opacity: 0.55;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .thesis-prose--warm::before {
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      rgba(157, 87, 40, 0.55),
      rgba(157, 87, 40, 0) 70%
    );
  }

  .thesis-prose--cool::before {
    background: radial-gradient(
      ellipse at center,
      rgba(33, 71, 60, 0.5),
      rgba(33, 71, 60, 0) 70%
    );
  }

  /* ----- "forces" emphasis — soft glow underline -------------------------- */

  .thesis-emphasis {
    position: relative;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0 0.04em;
  }

  .thesis-emphasis::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.05em;
    right: 0.05em;
    bottom: -0.08em;
    height: 0.32em;
    z-index: -1;
    border-radius: 999px;
    filter: blur(2px);
  }

  .thesis-emphasis--warm {
    color: #9d5728;
  }

  .thesis-emphasis--warm::after {
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(157, 87, 40, 0.32), rgba(157, 87, 40, 0));
  }

  .thesis-emphasis--cool {
    color: #21473c;
  }

  .thesis-emphasis--cool::after {
    background: linear-gradient(240deg, rgba(33, 71, 60, 0.28), rgba(33, 71, 60, 0));
  }

  /* ----- Below-fold cards (unchanged) ------------------------------------ */

  .summary-card {
    border: 1px solid rgba(24, 33, 38, 0.08);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    background: rgba(252, 250, 245, 0.88);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    box-shadow:
      0 8px 24px rgba(24, 33, 38, 0.06),
      0 1px 2px rgba(24, 33, 38, 0.05);
  }

  .summary-card__number {
    display: inline-flex;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #9d5728;
  }

  .summary-card h2 {
    font-family: 'Iowan Old Style', 'Palatino Linotype', 'Book Antiqua', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #182126;
  }

  .summary-card p {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #47616d;
  }
</style>
